    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0900" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg812"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Grip.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I had the honor to receive
                    yesterday afternoon your note of the 9th instant, requesting the good offices of
                    this Government for the Norwegian steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Hugin</hi>
                    upon her arrival at the port of Macoris, Santo Domingo.</p>
                <p>In reply it gives me pleasure to say that I have already brought this matter to
                    the attention of the Navy Department, having communicated <pb facs="0901"
                        n="813" xml:id="pg813"/> to that Department yesterday a request of Messrs.
                    Hugh Kelly &amp; Co. for the protection of the steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hugin</hi>.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
